// =====================================================================================
//  EXTERNAL EVENT SYSTEM — Part 1: offers (Event Board / Direct Offers), selection modes, details,
//  participant selection, calendar, preparation, Theater exception, persistent event artwork
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  · S.xe = {v, seq, list:[records], orgs:{id:organizer}, rep:{co, g:{gid}}, gen}
//    A record is an offer from the Event Board (ch 'board'), a Direct Offer (ch 'direct') or a Music
//    Program appearance (ch 'mp', Part 2). Status: open → accepted → done | declined | expired | cancelled.
//  · Selection mode is fixed by the event: events with a Live Performance use PLAYER selection (members from
//    the requested groups / teams; a senior (main) group also covers its sister groups); every other booking
//    uses ORGANIZER selection (named members, accept or decline only). No whole-group booking.
//  · Fixed payment only (shown before accepting). Offers never conflict with Concerts, Roadshows, other
//    external events or other locked activities; Theater does not block. Accepted events are stored as
//    schedule reservations (gsSched) so every system sees them, and members are unavailable for that day's
//    Theater performances → the existing Theater replacement / cancellation rules apply.
//  · Artwork: a stored spec (category scene + member snapshots) is created once per record and rendered
//    with the existing character art; it stays with the record (History) after save / load.
// =====================================================================================
